- How would you scale gating across multiple model_versions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a streaming, fault-tolerant, near-real-time cca_score system with intermittent connectivity. Focus on API surfaces, data models, ordering guarantees, and safe rollout.

## Key Concepts

- Streaming ingestion, sliding windows, watermarks
- Idempotency, replay protection, sequence numbering
- Latency targets, late/partitioned updates handling
- Canary rollouts, feature flags, monitoring and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Idempotent batch apply
function applyBatch(state, batch) {
  if (state.seenBatches.has(batch.batch_id)) return state;
  state.seenBatches.add(batch.batch_id);
  const total = state.total * state.count + batch.score;
  state.count += 1;
  state.total = total;
  state.globalScore = state.total / state.count;
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to bound staleness in the global score with late updates?
- How to design tests simulating network partitions and clock skew?

## Why This Is Asked
Explains how to add observability and robust failure handling in a real API, a common beginner hurdle as systems scale.

## Key Concepts
- Distributed tracing, metrics, circuit breakers
- Idempotency and retry strategies
- Canary rollout and failover testing

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight circuit-breaker sketch
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold=5, windowMs=60000) { this.failures=0; this.threshold=threshold; this.open=false; }
  recordFailure(){ this.failures++; if(this.failures>this.threshold){ this.open=true; setTimeout(()=>{ this.open=false; this.failures=0; }, 30000);} }
  canProceed(){ return !this.open; }
}
```

